IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-revision.l4: Chapter 11, ss 454 to 457 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): voluntary revision of accounts and
-- reports, the Secretary of State's notice, the application to court and the persons authorised to apply.
-- Lines 6145-6219 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the rule; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Provisions that address only the Secretary of State or the court are encoded for what they mean to the directors.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 454: voluntary revision of accounts etc
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6149 | (a) the company's annual accounts,
-- src:6150 | (b) the directors' remuneration report or the directors' report, or
-- src:6151 | (c) a strategic report of the company,
@ref s 454(1) The documents the directors may revise (src:6149-6151)
DECLARE `s 454 kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 454 the company's annual accounts`
    `s 454 the directors' remuneration report`
    `s 454 the directors' report`
    `s 454 a strategic report of the company`
    `s 454 another document`

-- src:6148 | (1) If it appears to the directors of a company that—
-- src:6149 | (a) the company's annual accounts,
-- src:6150 | (b) the directors' remuneration report or the directors' report, or
-- src:6151 | (c) a strategic report of the company,
-- src:6152 | did not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., they may prepare revised accounts or a revised report or statement.
@ref s 454(1) If it appears to the directors that a document did not comply, they may prepare a revised one (src:6148-6152)
GIVEN document IS A `s 454 kind of document`
      `it appears to the directors that the document did not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 454(1) the directors may prepare revised accounts or a revised report or statement` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `s 454 another document`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section lists the annual accounts, the directors' remuneration report or directors' report, and a strategic report
    ELSE IF `it appears to the directors that the document did not comply with the requirements of this Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the directors that ... did not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., they may prepare revised accounts or a revised report or statement."

-- src:6153 | (2) Where copies of the previous accounts or report have been sent out to members, delivered to the registrar or (in the case of a public company) laid before the company in general meeting, the revisions must be confined to—
@ref s 454(2) Where copies have gone out, the revisions are confined (does the confinement apply?) (src:6153)
GIVEN `copies of the previous accounts or report have been sent out to members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies of the previous accounts or report have been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the previous accounts or report have been laid before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 454(2) the revisions are confined to correction and consequential alterations` MEANS
    IF `copies of the previous accounts or report have been sent out to members`
       OR `copies of the previous accounts or report have been delivered to the registrar`
       OR (`the company is a public company` AND `the previous accounts or report have been laid before the company in general meeting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where copies of the previous accounts or report have been sent out to members, delivered to the registrar or (in the case of a public company) laid before the company in general meeting, the revisions must be confined to"

-- src:6153 | (2) Where copies of the previous accounts or report have been sent out to members, delivered to the registrar or (in the case of a public company) laid before the company in general meeting, the revisions must be confined to—
-- src:6154 | (a) the correction of those respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., and
-- src:6155 | (b) the making of any necessary consequential alterations.
@ref s 454(2) The revisions must be confined to correction and necessary consequential alterations (src:6153-6155)
GIVEN `s 454(2) the revisions are confined to correction and consequential alterations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the revisions consist only of the correction of those respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act and the making of any necessary consequential alterations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 454(2) the revision is within the limit the section sets` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 454(2) the revisions are confined to correction and consequential alterations`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the revisions consist only of the correction of those respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act and the making of any necessary consequential alterations`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the revisions must be confined to— (a) the correction of those respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., and (b) the making of any necessary consequential alterations"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the confinement applies only "Where copies of the previous accounts or report have been sent out ..."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the confinement applies is not known

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 455: Secretary of State's notice in respect of accounts or reports
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6172 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:6173 | (a) copies of a company's annual accounts , strategic report or directors’ report have been sent out under section 423, or
-- src:6174 | (b) a copy of a company's annual accounts , strategic report or directors’ report has been delivered to the registrar or (in the case of a public company) laid before the company in general meeting,
-- src:6175 | and it appears to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question whether the accounts or report comply with the requirements of this Act ....
@ref s 455(1) Where the section applies (src:6172-6175)
GIVEN `copies of the company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report have been sent out under section 423` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report has been delivered to the registrar or (in the case of a public company) laid before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question whether the accounts or report comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455(1) section 455 applies` MEANS
    IF (`copies of the company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report have been sent out under section 423`
        OR `a copy of the company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report has been delivered to the registrar or (in the case of a public company) laid before the company in general meeting`)
       AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question whether the accounts or report comply with the requirements of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "This section applies where— (a) copies ... have been sent out under section 423, or (b) a copy ... has been delivered to the registrar or ... laid before the company in general meeting, and it appears to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question"

-- src:6176 | (2) The Secretary of State may give notice to the directors of the company indicating the respects in which it appears that such a question arises or may arise.
@ref s 455(2) The Secretary of State may give the directors notice (src:6176)
GIVEN `s 455(1) section 455 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455(2) the Secretary of State may give notice to the directors indicating the respects in which a question arises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 455(1) section 455 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given only where the section applies
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

-- "a period of not less than one month": one calendar month from the date of the notice, by the daydate library's
-- `add months` (it clamps to the last day of a shorter month; the text gives no rule for counting this month, fork F10).
-- src:6177 | (3) The notice must specify a period of not less than one month for the directors to give an explanation of the accounts or report or prepare revised accounts or a revised report.
@ref s 455(3) The notice must specify a period of not less than one month (src:6177)
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period the notice specifies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455(3) the period the notice specifies is not less than one month` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period the notice specifies` AT LEAST (`add months` `the date of the notice` 1)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must specify a period of not less than one month"

-- (4): "at the end of the specified period, or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow ... it appears ... that the
-- directors have not (a) given a satisfactory explanation, or (b) revised the accounts or report": read as: have done neither (fork F11).
-- src:6178 | (4) If at the end of the specified period, or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow, it appears to the Secretary of State that the directors have not—
-- src:6179 | (a) given a satisfactory explanation of the accounts or report, or
-- src:6180 | (b) revised the accounts or report so as to comply with the requirements of this Act ...,
-- src:6181 | the Secretary of State may apply to the court.
@ref s 455(4) The Secretary of State may apply to the court (src:6178-6181)
GIVEN `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the end of the specified period, or of such longer period as the Secretary of State has allowed` IS A DATE
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the directors have given a satisfactory explanation of the accounts or report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the directors have revised the accounts or report so as to comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455(4) the Secretary of State may apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the question is asked` LESS THAN `the end of the specified period, or of such longer period as the Secretary of State has allowed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05): "If at the end of the specified period, or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow"
    ELSE IF `it appears to the Secretary of State that the directors have given a satisfactory explanation of the accounts or report`
            OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that the directors have revised the accounts or report so as to comply with the requirements of this Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "If" not met): "If at the end of the specified period ... it appears to the Secretary of State that the directors have not— (a) given a satisfactory explanation of the accounts or report, or (b) revised the accounts or report so as to comply"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5): the section applies equally to revised accounts and reports, with "revised" read as "further revised".
DECLARE `s 455 kind of revised document` IS ONE OF
    `s 455 revised annual accounts`
    `s 455 a revised strategic report`
    `s 455 a revised directors' report`
    `s 455 another revised document`

-- src:6182 | (5) The provisions of this section apply equally to revised annual accounts , revised strategic reports and revised directors’ reports, in which case they have effect as if the references to revised accounts or reports were references to further revised accounts or reports.
@ref s 455(5) The section applies equally to revised annual accounts, strategic reports and directors' reports (src:6182)
GIVEN document IS A `s 455 kind of revised document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455(5) section 455 applies equally to the revised document` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `s 455 another revised document`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "revised annual accounts, revised strategic reports and revised directors' reports"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "they have effect as if the references to revised accounts or reports were references to further revised accounts or reports".
-- src:6182 | (5) The provisions of this section apply equally to revised annual accounts , revised strategic reports and revised directors’ reports, in which case they have effect as if the references to revised accounts or reports were references to further revised accounts or reports.
@ref s 455(5) References to revised accounts or reports are read as references to further revised ones (src:6182)
GIVEN `the document the section is being applied to is itself a revised document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455(5) the references to revised accounts or reports are read as references to further revised accounts or reports` MEANS
    IF `the document the section is being applied to is itself a revised document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case they have effect as if" applies only to revised annual accounts, strategic reports and directors' reports

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 456: application to court in respect of defective accounts or reports
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6185 | (1) An application may be made to the court—
-- src:6186 | (a) by the Secretary of State, after having complied with section 455, or
-- src:6187 | (b) by a person authorised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this section,
@ref s 456(1) Who may apply to the court (src:6185-6187)
DECLARE `s 456 kind of applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 456 the Secretary of State, who has complied with section 455`
    `s 456 the Secretary of State, who has not complied with section 455`
    `s 456 a person authorised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of section 456`
    `s 456 any other person`

-- src:6185 | (1) An application may be made to the court—
-- src:6186 | (a) by the Secretary of State, after having complied with section 455, or
-- src:6187 | (b) by a person authorised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this section,
-- src:6188 | for a declaration (in Scotland, a declarator) that the annual accounts of a company do not comply,or a strategic report or a directors' report does not comply, with the requirements of this Act ... and for an order requiring the directors of the company to prepare revised accounts or a revised report.
@ref s 456(1) An application may be made to the court by the Secretary of State or an authorised person (src:6185-6188)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 456 kind of applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(1) the applicant may apply to the court for a declaration and an order` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 456 the Secretary of State, who has complied with section 455` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 456 a person authorised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of section 456` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 456 the Secretary of State, who has not complied with section 455` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the Secretary of State, after having complied with section 455"
    WHEN `s 456 any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names the Secretary of State and persons he has authorised, and does not say "only"

-- src:6189 | (2) Notice of the application, together with a general statement of the matters at issue in the proceedings, shall be given by the applicant to the registrar for registration.
@ref s 456(2) The applicant must give notice of the application to the registrar (src:6189)
GIVEN `the applicant has given the registrar notice of the application, with a general statement of the matters at issue in the proceedings, for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(2) the applicant has given the registrar the notice the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the applicant has given the registrar notice of the application, with a general statement of the matters at issue in the proceedings, for registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "shall" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "Notice of the application, together with a general statement of the matters at issue in the proceedings, shall be given by the applicant to the registrar for registration."

-- (3) and (4): the directions the court may give.
-- src:6190 | (3) If the court orders the preparation of revised accounts, it may give directions as to—
-- src:6191 | (a) the auditing of the accounts,
-- src:6192 | (b) the revision of any directors' remuneration report, strategic report and supplementary material or, directors' report ..., and
-- src:6193 | (c) the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous accounts,
-- src:6194 | and such other matters as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 456(3) Directions where the court orders revised accounts (src:6190-6194)
DECLARE `s 456 kind of direction` IS ONE OF
    `s 456 as to the auditing of the accounts`
    `s 456 as to the revision of any directors' remuneration report, strategic report and supplementary material or directors' report`
    `s 456 as to the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous accounts or report`
    `s 456 as to the review of the report by the auditors`
    `s 456 as to another matter`

-- src:6190 | (3) If the court orders the preparation of revised accounts, it may give directions as to—
-- src:6191 | (a) the auditing of the accounts,
-- src:6192 | (b) the revision of any directors' remuneration report, strategic report and supplementary material or, directors' report ..., and
-- src:6193 | (c) the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous accounts,
-- src:6194 | and such other matters as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 456(3) The court may give directions where it orders the preparation of revised accounts (src:6190-6194)
GIVEN `the court orders the preparation of revised accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      direction IS A `s 456 kind of direction`
      `the court thinks fit to give a direction on another matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(3) the court may give the direction` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court orders the preparation of revised accounts`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court orders the preparation of revised accounts, it may give directions as to"
    ELSE CONSIDER direction
         WHEN `s 456 as to the auditing of the accounts` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 456 as to the revision of any directors' remuneration report, strategic report and supplementary material or directors' report` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 456 as to the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous accounts or report` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 456 as to the review of the report by the auditors` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the direction named in subsection (4)(a) is not in subsection (3)'s list
         WHEN `s 456 as to another matter` THEN
             IF `the court thinks fit to give a direction on another matter`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "such other matters as the court thinks fit" is the court's judgment

-- src:6195 | (4) If the court orders the preparation of a revised strategic report or directors' report it may give directions as to—
-- src:6196 | (a) the review of the report by the auditors,
-- src:6197 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:6198 | (c) the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous report, and
-- src:6199 | (d) such other matters as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 456(4) The court may give directions where it orders a revised strategic report or directors' report (src:6195-6199)
GIVEN `the court orders the preparation of a revised strategic report or directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      direction IS A `s 456 kind of direction`
      `the court thinks fit to give a direction on another matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(4) the court may give the direction` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court orders the preparation of a revised strategic report or directors' report`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court orders the preparation of a revised strategic report or directors' report it may give directions as to"
    ELSE CONSIDER direction
         WHEN `s 456 as to the review of the report by the auditors` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 456 as to the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous accounts or report` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 456 as to the auditing of the accounts` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the direction named in subsection (3)(a) is not in subsection (4)'s list
         WHEN `s 456 as to the revision of any directors' remuneration report, strategic report and supplementary material or directors' report` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the direction named in subsection (3)(b) is not in subsection (4)'s list
         WHEN `s 456 as to another matter` THEN
             IF `the court thinks fit to give a direction on another matter`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "such other matters as the court thinks fit" is the court's judgment

-- (5): the costs and expenses of the application and of preparing revised accounts "are to be borne by such of the directors as
-- were party to the approval"; every director at the time of the approval is taken to have been a party unless he shows that he
-- took all reasonable steps to prevent it. "unless he shows" is an "unless" once met: decided at this site (ruling of 2026-11-05).
-- src:6204 | For this purpose every director of the company at the time of the approval of the accounts or report shall be taken to have been a party to the approval unless he shows that he took all reasonable steps to prevent that approval.
@ref s 456(5) Every director at the time of the approval is taken to have been a party to it, unless he shows he took all reasonable steps to prevent it (src:6204)
GIVEN `the person was a director of the company at the time of the approval of the accounts or report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director shows that he took all reasonable steps to prevent that approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(5) the director is taken to have been a party to the approval of the defective accounts or report` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person was a director of the company at the time of the approval of the accounts or report`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every director of the company at the time of the approval"
    ELSE IF `the director shows that he took all reasonable steps to prevent that approval`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "unless" met): "unless he shows that he took all reasonable steps to prevent that approval"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:6200 | (5) If the court finds that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act ...it may order that all or part of—
-- src:6201 | (a) the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of and incidental to the application, and
-- src:6202 | (b) any reasonable expenses incurred by the company in connection with or in consequence of the preparation of revised accounts or a revised report,
-- src:6203 | are to be borne by such of the directors as were party to the approval of the defective accounts or report.
@ref s 456(5) The court may order the directors who were party to the approval to bear the costs and expenses (src:6200-6203)
GIVEN `the court finds that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 456(5) the director is taken to have been a party to the approval of the defective accounts or report` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(5) the court may order that the director bear the costs and expenses` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court finds that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court finds that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act ... it may order"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 456(5) the director is taken to have been a party to the approval of the defective accounts or report`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "are to be borne by such of the directors as were party to the approval of the defective accounts or report"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order reaches only directors who were party to the approval

-- src:6205 | (6) Where the court makes an order under subsection (5) it shall have regard to whether the directors party to the approval of the defective accounts or report knew or ought to have known that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., and it may exclude one or more directors from the order or order the payment of different amounts by different directors.
@ref s 456(6) The court may exclude a director or order different amounts (src:6205)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(6) the court may exclude one or more directors from the order or order the payment of different amounts` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where the court makes an order under subsection (5) it shall have regard to ... and it may exclude one or more directors from the order or order the payment of different amounts by different directors."

-- src:6205 | (6) Where the court makes an order under subsection (5) it shall have regard to whether the directors party to the approval of the defective accounts or report knew or ought to have known that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., and it may exclude one or more directors from the order or order the payment of different amounts by different directors.
@ref s 456(6) The matter the court must have regard to: whether the director knew or ought to have known (src:6205)
GIVEN `the director knew that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director ought to have known that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 456(6) the director knew or ought to have known that the accounts or report did not comply` MEANS
    `the director knew that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act` OR `the director ought to have known that the accounts or report did not comply with the requirements of this Act`

-- (7): at the end of the proceedings the applicant must send the registrar a copy of the court order, or notice that the
-- application failed or was withdrawn. The text states no time, so the rule has no WITHIN. The parties are the text's own.
DECLARE `s 456 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 456 the applicant`
    `s 456 the registrar`

DECLARE `s 456 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 456 send to the registrar for registration a copy of the court order`
    `s 456 give notice to the registrar that the application has failed or been withdrawn`

DECLARE `s 456 outcome of the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 456 the court made an order`
    `s 456 the application failed`
    `s 456 the application was withdrawn`

-- src:6206 | (7) On the conclusion of proceedings on an application under this section, the applicant must send to the registrar for registration a copy of the court order or, as the case may be, give notice to the registrar that the application has failed or been withdrawn.
@ref s 456(7) On the conclusion of proceedings the applicant must send the registrar the order or notice of failure or withdrawal (src:6206)
GIVEN outcome IS A `s 456 outcome of the proceedings`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 456 party` `s 456 act`
`s 456(7) the applicant's duty to inform the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN `s 456 the court made an order` THEN
        PARTY `s 456 the applicant`
        MUST `s 456 send to the registrar for registration a copy of the court order`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 456 the applicant` BECAUSE "s 456(7): no copy of the court order was sent to the registrar for registration"
    OTHERWISE
        PARTY `s 456 the applicant`
        MUST `s 456 give notice to the registrar that the application has failed or been withdrawn`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 456 the applicant` BECAUSE "s 456(7): no notice was given to the registrar that the application had failed or been withdrawn"

-- src:6206 | (7) On the conclusion of proceedings on an application under this section, the applicant must send to the registrar for registration a copy of the court order or, as the case may be, give notice to the registrar that the application has failed or been withdrawn.
@ref s 456(7) The applicant has done what the section requires of him (src:6206)
GIVEN outcome IS A `s 456 outcome of the proceedings`
      `the applicant has sent the registrar a copy of the court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has given the registrar notice that the application has failed or been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(7) the applicant has complied` MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN `s 456 the court made an order` THEN
        IF `the applicant has sent the registrar a copy of the court order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "the applicant must send to the registrar for registration a copy of the court order"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the applicant has given the registrar notice that the application has failed or been withdrawn`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "give notice to the registrar that the application has failed or been withdrawn"

-- src:6207 | (8) The provisions of this section apply equally to revised annual accounts , revised strategic reports and revised directors’ reports, in which case they have effect as if the references to revised accounts or reports were references to further revised accounts or reports.
@ref s 456(8) The section applies equally to revised annual accounts, strategic reports and directors' reports (src:6207)
GIVEN document IS A `s 455 kind of revised document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456(8) section 456 applies equally to the revised document` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `s 455 another revised document`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "revised annual accounts, revised strategic reports and revised directors' reports"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 457: other persons authorised to apply to the court
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 457(1)-(3), (5)-(7) are the Secretary of State's order-making power to authorise persons and its limits: machinery
-- (inert, reason 2). (4) says who sues and is sued when the authorised person is an unincorporated association.

-- src:6215 | (4) If the authorised person is an unincorporated association, proceedings brought in, or in connection with, the exercise of any function by the association as an authorised person may be brought by or against the association in the name of a body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the association.
@ref s 457(4) Proceedings by or against an authorised unincorporated association (src:6215)
GIVEN `the authorised person is an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought in, or in connection with, the exercise of any function by the association as an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate's constitution provides for the establishment of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 457(4) the proceedings may be brought by or against the association in the name of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF NOT `the authorised person is an unincorporated association`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the authorised person is an unincorporated association, proceedings brought in, or in connection with, the exercise of any function by the association as an authorised person may be brought by or against the association in the name of a body corporate"
    ELSE IF NOT `the proceedings are brought in, or in connection with, the exercise of any function by the association as an authorised person`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings brought in, or in connection with, the exercise of any function by the association as an authorised person"
         ELSE IF `the body corporate's constitution provides for the establishment of the association`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the name of a body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the association"
